Cape Verde advanced to the knockout stages of the World Cup on their debut appearance following a 0-0 draw with Saudi Arabia on Friday night in Houston.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9614b20a-71cf-11f1-b6b6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/cape-verde-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9614b20a-71cf-11f1-b6b6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/cape-verde-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aae5b8b4-71cf-11f1-93a4-cb20d4461437</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 02:39:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9614b20a-71cf-11f1-b6b6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/cape-verde-1.jpg">REUTERS - Annegret Hilse</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Punishing heatwave exposes cracks in France's nuclear power fleet</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260626-punishing-heatwave-exposes-cracks-in-france-s-nuclear-power-fleet-reactor</link><description>
Three French nuclear plants halted production during this week's record-breaking heatwave as rivers became too warm to cool them, raising questions over the long-term future of Europe's biggest nuclear fleet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5f2d494c-10b9-11ea-819d-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-18t000000z_1975114624_rc19d5eae900_rtrmadp_3_edf-nuclearpower_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5f2d494c-10b9-11ea-819d-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-18t000000z_1975114624_rc19d5eae900_rtrmadp_3_edf-nuclearpower_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6176a34-707c-11f1-a529-c7d93de76560</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 16:00:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5f2d494c-10b9-11ea-819d-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-18t000000z_1975114624_rc19d5eae900_rtrmadp_3_edf-nuclearpower_0.jpg">REUTERS/Benoit Tessier</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Israel's targeting of Gaza's children proves genocidal intent, UN inquiry finds</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260626-israel-s-targeting-of-gaza-children-proves-genocidal-intent-un-inquiry-says</link><description>
The deliberate targeting of Palestinian children is central to a United Nations-mandated report's conclusion that Israel is committing genocide in Gaza. The commission argues that children have not only been victims of the war, but have been targeted in ways that help establish genocidal intent. Israel has dismissed the findings of the report, released this week, as "defamatory".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0862b8a8-493a-11f0-a15b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25140303784353.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0862b8a8-493a-11f0-a15b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25140303784353.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0356a1c0-714e-11f1-9c0f-bf9829427aa8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 15:01:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0862b8a8-493a-11f0-a15b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25140303784353.jpg">© Abdel Kareem Hana / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France heatwave overwhelms hospitals and forces Pride march delay</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260626-france-heatwave-overwhelms-hospitals-and-forces-pride-march-delay</link><description>
Emergency doctors at one of Paris's biggest hospitals warned on Friday that wards had become dangerously overcrowded after a week of soaring temperatures, as authorities restricted public alcohol consumption, organisers postponed the annual Pride march and €130 million was pledged to help schools adapt to climate change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/101e5bf2-7129-11f1-8777-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7YK4EB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/101e5bf2-7129-11f1-8777-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7YK4EB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b6d965e-7139-11f1-bcba-b7d731ab2001</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 10:11:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/101e5bf2-7129-11f1-8777-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7YK4EB.jpg">AFP - SEBASTIEN SALOM-GOMIS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Current Europe heatwave 'impossible' without human-induced climate change</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260626-europe-heatwave-virtually-impossible-without-human-caused-climate-change</link><description>
A study comparing the heatwave that has swept across Europe this week with heatwaves in 1976 and 2003 has found that human-caused climate change is "unequivocally" responsible for the extreme heat over the last week – with France recording its hottest day since records began in 1947 on Wednesday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/027f5fe8-70c3-11f1-8b7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8246NT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/027f5fe8-70c3-11f1-8b7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8246NT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a7bd136-7125-11f1-9a8e-01fd4a7e37ad</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 07:06:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/027f5fe8-70c3-11f1-8b7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8246NT.jpg">AFP - DIMITAR DILKOFF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Calls for child protection reforms in wake of schoolgirl Lyhanna's death</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260626-calls-for-child-protection-reforms-in-wake-of-schoolgirl-lyhanna-s-death</link><description>
An investigation into previous child rape allegations against the suspect in the death of a schoolgirl in southern France has revealed failures by prosecutors and police. The case has unleashed a wave of criticism over how sexual and gender-based violence cases are handled in France, with victims, families and advocates pushing for reform.
